Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.19,0:03:20.45,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,I will now explain the \Nrules of the class vote.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.18,0:03:24.72,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,In four days, you will \Nevaluate your classmates,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.72,0:03:27.48,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,voting for three students \Nwho are worthy of praise,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.92,0:03:32.45,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,and three students who are worthy of censure.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.48,0:03:38.47,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,The student with the most positive \Nvotes will receive a special reward—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.47,0:03:42.49,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,a new privilege known \Nas a "protection point."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.49,0:03:44.50,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,A protection point?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.50,0:03:49.25,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,It allows its user to negate an \Nexpulsion they've qualified for.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.25,0:03:50.31,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,You kidding me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.31,0:03:50.80,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,Wow!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.63,0:03:52.75,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,That's awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.80,0:03:52.75,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,That's amazing!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.99,0:03:52.02,Main_Top,Shinohara,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.02,0:03:54.23,Main_Top,Sato,0,0,0,,That's the best privilege ever!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.69,0:03:56.37,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That's a rather extreme reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.20,0:04:01.01,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Does something negative happen \Nto the three lowest placers?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.01,0:04:03.56,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Only one of them will be affected.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.18,0:04:07.37,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,The purpose of the exam is \Nto total up votes received,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.37,0:04:11.48,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,with positive votes adding points \Nand negative votes subtracting them,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.48,0:04:14.28,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,to determine a single top \Nand single bottom placer.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.70,0:04:16.53,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,The single... bottom placer?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.91,0:04:23.12,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,As for why the school is using the \Nextraordinary measure of protection points...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.48,0:04:27.79,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,It's because this is one test \Nthat most likely cannot end
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.79,0:04:30.21,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,without someone getting expelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.88,0:04:34.12,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,That's right. The lowest placing student...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.37,0:04:37.97,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,will be expelled from this school.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.47,0:04:41.83,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,Huh? Expelled?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.22,0:04:42.50,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,No freaking way!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.83,0:04:44.43,Main,Shinohara,0,0,0,,After we passed, even...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.50,0:04:43.56,Main,Wang,0,0,0,,It can't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.43,0:04:45.22,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,In addition,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.54,0:04:49.30,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,the protection point received \Nby the highest placing student
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.30,0:04:51.98,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,cannot be transferred to others.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.98,0:04:55.78,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Which means someone will \Nbe expelled for sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.06,0:05:01.62,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Though simple, this may \Nbe the cruelest test yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.62,0:05:03.72,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,I don't get this!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.72,0:05:06.62,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,Are we seriously talking \Nabout expelling someone?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.83,0:05:07.71,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.11,0:05:13.03,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,But for once, the class will not be \Npenalized when the expulsion takes place.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.03,0:05:16.38,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,The expulsion itself {\i1}is{\i0} the penalty!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.38,0:05:19.26,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,A protection point is \Nan extraordinary reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.24,0:05:26.39,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,But it comes with an appropriately \Nextraordinary risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.60,0:05:29.14,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,I fully understand that \Nyou find it unreasonable.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.64,0:05:33.39,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,But now that it's done, \Nyou must follow the rules,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.39,0:05:35.38,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,and undertake the special exam.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.89,0:05:37.90,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,That's how the world works.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.68,0:05:41.66,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Sakayanagi's father, the chairman,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.66,0:05:45.32,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,didn't seem like the type to \Nconduct unreasonable exams, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.32,0:05:47.75,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Let's not lose hope just yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.75,0:05:49.81,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,We've always found a way through before.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.81,0:05:52.58,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,There's got to be a way to \Nprevent expulsion this time!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.99,0:05:54.91,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Hirata-kun is right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.91,0:06:00.71,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,We need to come together as a class and \Nmake sure all the votes come out equally.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.71,0:06:03.38,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,No, that won't help you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.38,0:06:09.10,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,You'll be forced to repeat the \Nvote until someone is expelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.84,0:06:14.74,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,In addition, you'll be casting one positive \Nvote for a student in another class.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.45,0:06:19.84,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,So it will be impossible for a single \Nclass to fully manipulate the result.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.40,0:06:24.12,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,But earlier, you said "most likely" expelled...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.12,0:06:28.24,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,The use of private points \Ncould change the equation.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.52,0:06:34.37,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,If you can pay twenty million points, \Nyou can potentially cancel an expulsion.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.66,0:06:36.63,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Twenty million points?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.63,0:06:40.53,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,That's way too many points \Nto pool for one person!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.53,0:06:44.13,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,Which means, after the test, \Nsomeone from this class is...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.04,0:06:47.28,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,What the heck are we gonna do?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.28,0:06:50.31,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,This is the worst test possible!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.84,0:06:50.31,Main,Shinohara,0,0,0,,Shut up, Yamauchi!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.31,0:06:51.37,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,What's your problem?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.37,0:06:54.27,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,Hey... you're not gonna cast a \Nnegative vote for me, are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.27,0:06:56.75,Main,Sato,0,0,0,,She's not gonna tell you who she's voting for.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.75,0:06:58.58,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,Yeah, I knew it!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.58,0:07:01.60,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,I guess I'll have to vote for you guys, then!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.60,0:07:03.53,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,How unsightly.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.53,0:07:08.53,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,This is a test about looking \Nforward at our next two years.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.53,0:07:11.66,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Well, you're not exactly \Nin a safe spot, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.87,0:07:15.89,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,You understand so little, Red Hair-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.89,0:07:16.60,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.60,0:07:18.88,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,The fact that there's no penalty to the class
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.88,0:07:23.30,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,makes it an excellent opportunity \Nto delete an undesirable classmate.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.30,0:07:26.77,Main,Koenji,0,0,0,,Such as one of your incompetent \Nfriends, perhaps.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.77,0:07:27.74,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,Incompetent?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.74,0:07:28.80,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,Shut the hell up!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.80,0:07:31.31,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Calm down. Let's all stay cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.31,0:07:32.95,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,You don't have to worry, Hirata!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.95,0:07:35.86,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,It's not like you're gonna \Nend up on the bottom!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.86,0:07:36.44,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,Hey—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.44,0:07:39.25,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,You're the safest one here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.25,0:07:41.32,Main,Hirata,0,0,0,,It's not guaranteed for me, either!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.32,0:07:44.31,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,It's not guaranteed for you, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.31,0:07:46.82,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,Yeah, right. You're the one safe man here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.82,0:07:48.90,Main,Yamauchi,0,0,0,,Sure is nice being popular, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.90,0:07:51.33,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,Yeah, he doesn't have to \Nworry about being expelled!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.78,0:07:51.33,Main_Top,Wang,0,0,0,,Hirata-kun...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.54,0:07:53.53,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Yeah, so just back off.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.53,0:07:55.11,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,I'm talking to Koenji right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.11,0:07:56.83,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,That's enough, Sudo-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.05,0:07:58.47,Main,Sudo,0,0,0,,Suzune?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.47,0:08:00.67,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,There's still some time before the vote.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.04,0:08:03.34,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Let's use that time to think up what to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.34,0:08:08.09,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,As I'm sure you're aware, blank votes \Nand abstentions will not be allowed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.50,0:08:13.60,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Votes for yourself or multiple votes for \Nthe same person are also not allowed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.56,0:08:17.65,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,I understand that this test \Nwill be difficult for you,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.19,0:08:20.35,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,but these are the rules \Nas decided by the school.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.03,0:08:24.45,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,As long as you're attending this \Nschool, you must follow these rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.27,0:08:27.99,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Now, we will hold the vote in four days.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.64,0:08:29.74,Main,Chabashira,0,0,0,,Do you understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.74,0:08:31.74,Main,Ike,0,0,0,,You can't do this to us!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.30,0:08:36.50,Main,Hasebe,0,0,0,,Boy, this really stinks, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.50,0:08:39.37,Main,Miyake,0,0,0,,Isn't there any way to get around it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.59,0:08:42.42,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Planning out our votes is the only way.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.42,0:08:44.39,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,I do have a suggestion.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.39,0:08:47.26,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,What would you think about us \Ncoordinating our votes as a group?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.26,0:08:50.51,Main,Hasebe,0,0,0,,You mean, write each other \Nfor the positive votes?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.51,0:08:51.58,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.58,0:08:53.64,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,It won't guarantee us a place at the top,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.64,0:08:56.85,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,but cooperating to avoid placing \Nlast is probably for the best.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.19,0:08:59.18,Main,Sakura,0,0,0,,But is that all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.18,0:09:02.33,Main,Sakura,0,0,0,,The teacher said trying to arrange \Nthe vote wouldn't help.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.33,0:09:06.40,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Even if we don't do it, \Nother groups surely will.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.77,0:09:10.26,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'm in favor of covering \Nfor each other as a group.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.82,0:09:13.80,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I wouldn't want to lose anyone here.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.80,0:09:15.16,Main,Sakura,0,0,0,,N-Neither do I!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.16,0:09:16.66,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,It's settled, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.52,0:09:21.20,Main,Hasebe,0,0,0,,Then let's get ahead of the game \Nand talk to some others.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.20,0:09:25.75,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,No, we should stay under the \Nradar until the test is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.04,0:09:28.22,Main,Miyake,0,0,0,,So that we don't end up \Ndeliberately targeted?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.22,0:09:29.76,Main,Yukimura,0,0,0,,Yes. In this test,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.76,0:09:33.73,Main_Top,Yukimura,0,0,0,,if someone gets negative votes \Nfocused on them, there's no defense.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.19,0:09:31.56,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,In this test,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.09,0:09:37.28,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,the lowest in the class hierarchy will \Nlikely become negative vote sinks.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.73,0:09:37.76,Main_Top,Hasebe,0,0,0,,I see. We've got to lie low until the test, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.98,0:09:38.90,Main,Sakura,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.87,0:09:43.46,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I suppose I'll have to take action, then.
